# oracle: pair_coeff options of pair_style mgpt: nbody 23 (pair and three-ion terms only, a warning natively) and volpress no (no volume terms in the pressure), with the V6.1 potential (3x3x3 bcc V, displaced at random by up to 0.25 bohr), 3 NVE steps with thermo every step
# native: b332f28 built with -D PKG_MGPT=on -D PKG_MANYBODY=on -D PKG_MOLECULE=on (serial, 1 process, default CMake Release flags, so the MGPT generic linear algebra; the installed lmp lacks MGPT)
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 2.0e-15, atoms 0 (bit for bit).
# oracle-potentials: V6.1.mgpt.parmin V6.1.mgpt.potin
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
units           electron
atom_style      atomic
variable        atomic_vol equal 93.23
variable        lattice_constant equal (${atomic_vol}*2.0)^(1.0/3.0)
lattice         bcc ${lattice_constant}
region          box block 0 3 0 3 0 3
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
displace_atoms  all random 0.25 0.25 0.25 977 units box
pair_style      mgpt
pair_coeff      * * V6.1.mgpt.parmin V6.1.mgpt.potin ${atomic_vol} nbody 23 volpress no precision double
neighbor        0.3 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
fix             1 all nve
timestep        1.0
thermo          1
thermo_style    custom step pe ke press pxx pyy pzz pxy pxz pyz
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
run             3
